{
  "_about": "Desk styles from the Product Designer (design-drafts/desk-textures/spec.md, final 2026-11-08). Texture is the owner's Grok grain; in Light and Dark the colour is the MA palette's. In Zen (the dusk entries; ADR 0093 and its Ash grey addendum, 2026-11-12) the three wood desks are Ash grey, the owner's pick: the brown taken out, with the regrade's lightness, grain and status text, and a breath of the slate's blue (OKLab C 0.011, hue 270) so no pixel tips warm (design-drafts/cool-tints/, Ash grey). Linoleum is a steel-blue slate at the Zen slate's own chroma, unchanged. Zen desks sit on the Zen ground #4D5463: Light oak, Walnut and Linoleum under it, White ash a little lighter. White oak (Nov 15, the owner: \"a white oak, not quite as white as Plain but close ... with slight strands of very light and desat tan\", then \"Needs to be closer to white\") is the shipped oak grain graded near-white with faint tan only in its darker strands (design-drafts/desk-textures/white-oak/). In Light it takes Plain's cut tinted from the wood (letters darker than the desk, a white lip), since light letters can't read on a near-white desk. In Zen its inks have no warm hue and its field is a cool grey; only the grain keeps a hint of tan (ADR 0093, White oak addendum).",
  "default": "oak",
  "order": [
    "oak",
    "white-oak",
    "ash",
    "walnut",
    "linoleum"
  ],
  "scale": {
    "tilePx": 1024,
    "deskUnits": 512,
    "pxPerUnit": 2,
    "why": "One tile covers 512 desk units, so a 600-unit desk shows at most one repeat and the grain keeps the size the stills were judged at. Above 2 px per unit the image is magnified, which a soft grain hides. Anchor at the desk top-left, offset by a hash of the desk id mod 512 (spec, Filling the panel)."
  },
  "etchNotes": {
    "light": "light letters: fill lighter than the desk; wall is a 1 px darker line above each stroke; no highlight",
    "dusk": "Zen: medium letters in the wood's own hue, lighter than the desk inside 1.8 to 3:1 of the tile's mean; wall darker line above; no highlight",
    "dark": "dark letters: fill darker than the desk; the wall merges with the fill; the highlight (1 px lighter line below each stroke) is the line that reads, so fillVsGrooveLine is measured against highlight in Dark and against wall elsewhere"
  },
  "deskTextNotes": "deskText replaces text.secondary for text drawn on the desk (the strip status line). text.secondary fails 4.5:1 on mid-tone desks, and mid-tone desks are what the owner's etch rule needs (light letters must be lighter than the desk). In Zen all four desks hold text.secondary. moreContrast is for prefers-contrast: more.",
  "darkTiles": "In Dark, resting app tiles on a textured desk wear a 1 px rgba(255,255,255,0.12) edge (elevation.tileStacked).",
